      "text": "Gemini Decision 1 (gemini-decision-1) is a calibrated multimodal model from Google designed for fast, closed-set decision tasks. Unlike generative LLMs that produce open-ended text, it takes a single multimodal input (text, image, audio, video, or PDF up to 256K tokens) and a set of up to 1,000 independent questions, then returns structured decisions for each — such as tool selection, policy compliance, model routing, or context relevance scores. It is served through the Gemini Decisions API in Google AI Studio, offering deterministic, low-latency (~200 ms) inference at a fixed price per million input tokens. The model represents a new class of \"decision models\" optimized for agentic control flow rather than content generation."
