    "summary": "Google launched Gemini Decision 1, a calibrated multimodal decision model accessible via the new Gemini Decisions API in Google AI Studio. The model evaluates up to 1,000 independent questions in a single pass across text, images, audio, video, and PDFs (256K token context) with roughly 200 ms end-to-end latency at $0.10 per million input tokens. Sundar Pichai and Logan Kilpatrick announced the release, positioning it as the first production-grade decision model from a major lab — beating Anthropic to market. The API targets bounded-choice tasks such as tool selection, policy checks, model routing, and context grading, returning structured decisions rather than generated text. The launch coincides with broader industry focus on decision models as a new primitive for agentic workflows, and developers are already comparing it to the iPhone-era shift in AI device paradigms.",
